## ARCHITECTURE QUICK REFERENCE

### Directory Structure
```
SaneVideo/
├── Core/           # Foundation: Models, Protocols, Utilities, DI, Extensions
│   ├── AppError.swift     # Unified error handling
│   └── AppLogger.swift    # Centralized logging
├── Services/       # Business logic (20+ services)
│   ├── AI/         # OpenAI, Gemini, Apple Intelligence
│   ├── Audio/      # Processing, waveforms, voice isolation
│   ├── Camera/     # CameraManager
│   ├── Captions/   # Caption generation
│   ├── Export/     # ExportEngine
│   ├── Project/    # ProjectStore (persistence)
│   ├── Recording/  # RecordingEngine
│   ├── SmartFeatures/  # Magic Fix
│   ├── Thumbnails/ # Smart thumbnails
│   ├── Timeline/   # Timeline operations
│   └── Vision/     # Face tracking, segmentation, saliency
├── State/          # App state management
│   ├── AppState.swift
│   ├── ProjectState.swift + extensions
│   ├── RecordingState.swift
│   ├── PlaybackState.swift
│   └── CameraState.swift
├── Views/          # SwiftUI views, Components, Sheets
└── Windows/        # Custom windows (FloatingControls, PiP)
```

### Concurrency Model
- **@MainActor**: AppState, all ObservableObjects, UI updates
- **Actors**: For shared state in services
- **async/await**: Prefer over completion handlers
- **Background queues**: AVFoundation operations, file I/O

### Logging Categories
```swift
AppLogger.camera      // AVCapture operations
AppLogger.recording   // Recording lifecycle
AppLogger.export      // Export operations
AppLogger.timeline    // Timeline edits
AppLogger.project     // Persistence
AppLogger.uiLog       // UI events
AppLogger.general     // Everything else
```

---

## STYLE GUIDE

### Formatting
- **Line Length**: 120 chars max
- **Indent**: 4 spaces
- **Linting**: Enforced by `swiftlint`

### SwiftUI
- Use trailing closure syntax: `.background { Color.blue }`
- Extract complex views if body > 50 lines
- Use `@Observable` (Swift 5.9+) for state objects
- Use `Task { await ... }` instead of `DispatchQueue`

### Naming
- **Services**: `CameraManager`, `AudioService`
- **Views**: `VideoPlayerView`, `SettingsButton`
- **Actions**: `loadVideo()`, `saveProject()` (verbs)

### Error Handling
- Use `AppError` enum — never throw raw `NSError` or strings
- Handle errors at call site or propagate explicitly

---

## TROUBLESHOOTING

### Common Issues

| Problem | Solution |
|---------|----------|
| Ghost Beeps / No Launch | Run `xcodegen generate` |
| "Signal 9" Crash | Check `SaneVideo.entitlements` for App Sandbox |
| Phantom Errors | Run `./Scripts/SaneMaster.rb clean --nuclear` |
| Permissions Black Screen | Run `tccutil reset Camera` |

### Common Crash Patterns

| Pattern | Crash Signature | Root Cause | Fix |
|---------|-----------------|------------|-----|
| Actor Isolation | `MainActor.assumeIsolated → dispatch_assert_queue_fail` | Calling MainActor code from background | Remove `assumeIsolated` from `deinit`, use `nonisolated(unsafe)` |
| Object Deallocated | `objc_opt_class → swift_getObjectType → SIGSEGV at 0x1e` | Timer/Publisher accessing deallocated view | Use `TimelineView` instead of `Timer.publish()`, add `isActive` guards |
| Race Condition | `objc_release → SIGSEGV` at random addresses | Concurrent access to non-thread-safe property | Use `nonisolated(unsafe)` with direct initialization |
| Nested Tasks | Freeze at `_isSameExecutor` | Excessive actor hopping | Remove nested `Task { @MainActor in Task { @OtherActor in } }` |

### Key Warning Signs
- **Address 0x0-0x1000**: NULL pointer dereference (object deallocated)
- **faultingThread: 0**: Main thread crash (UI/state issue)
- **faultingThread: N > 0**: Background thread crash (concurrency issue)
- **EXC_BREAKPOINT (SIGTRAP)**: Swift assertion failed or `assumeIsolated` violation
- **EXC_BAD_ACCESS (SIGSEGV)**: Memory corruption or use-after-free

